<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 39.2 trln lira t-bills at 118.75 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 39.2 trln lira t-bills at 118.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 273-day t-bill auction of the Turkish Treasury on Tuesday produced the following results.</p>
<p>	Maturity		    : August 6, 1997</p>
<p>	Amount			: 39.23 trln lira</p>
<p>	Coupon			: -</p>
<p>	Minimum yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Maximum yield	     : 118.75</p>
<p>	Average yield	     : -</p>
<p>	Bid amount/cover	  : 244 trln</p>
<p>	Lowest accepted price   : 55,595 lira</p>
<p>Pct allocated at lowest price : -</p>
<p>	Payment date		: November 6, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - The central bank said the Treasury would sell t-bills and bonds at the maximum accepted yield, or the lowest accepted price in auctions from today onward due to a 10 percent witholding tax which newly went into effect on interest income from state securities.</p>
<p>The tax will be charged on interest earnings from t-bills and bonds to mature in 1997.</p>
<p>--Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75 EKS</p>
